## What this session accomplished

**Run74's wedge root-caused and fixed (FIX-3/4):** the `cnt=-510` forensic decoded as a reader-count *underflow*, not a leaked write lock — FIX-2's P3B audit loop was calling `mxfs_dir_flush_data_blocks_relsafe` (which consumes the caller's read hold) without holding it, corrupting the dir's rwsem by one unmatched `up_read` per iteration. Also bounded the release drain (180s → shutdown) so any future rwsem wedge degrades to fence-and-replay instead of a 400s cluster convoy.

**The write-suppression family unwound (FIX-5/6/7, proven via a live deterministic repro):** run75 exposed that dir-metadata `written_seq` was stamped at *submit* (the sess42 fix existed but was never enabled), so every "is this buffer undestaged?" safety check lied; NL-window write suppressors then dropped a grown dir block's only write and the release evict destroyed the in-core copy — leaving a **prior-mkfs image** on the platter (uuid-mismatch EFSCORRUPTED, reproducible across remount). Now: wseq stamps only at real bio completion, and no suppressor or evict path may touch an undestaged buffer.

**FUA-read transport hardened:** run76's mount-poisoning traced to the SCSI READ(16) passthrough returning silent EIO under storm queue pressure; it now retries with backoff and attributable logging (run77+: zero EIOs).

**Reload adopt-reverts closed (FIX-8/9):** captured live twice — a reload adopting the platter's older dinode while this node's own committed grow was still undestaged (reverting nx 7→6, then 9→1), corrupting the da-btree. The reload now refuses to run at all while the inode has logged-not-destaged core changes.

**FIX-10 (built as `BA67B6309C428709F33650A`, untested):** run80 captured the recurring "md5-wave tail lost" signature end-to-end — the anti-staleness platter-compare guard's undestaged exception only applied to AIL-resident buffers, so CIL-window fresh adds got invalidated+re-read from the platter, durably discarding them. The undestaged keep-guard is now unconditional.

## Where it stands

run79 scored **7/8** with the only failure a 12-entry readdir lag that self-healed within 2 seconds (rank1, round 7 — same node/round pattern recurred in run80, next suspect: the clean-skip PR release possibly bypassing the P3B fence). Next session: cycle the cluster onto `BA67B6309`, drive drc 8/tcp toward 5 consecutive passes, chase the rank1-round7 transient and the rank1 EDEADLK starvation (10,380 upgrade denials/run) if they persist, then run the full `./run.sh N tcp` matrix for N∈{8,4,2,1}. All details, evidence paths, and open leads are in ccmemory `sess5-FIVE-ROOT-FIXES-suppression-family-and-probes` and `sess5-END-run80-p28c-cil-window-fix10-built`.

